      "title": "Amcor September 2026-End Earnings Miss on Higher Costs, View Cut",
      "summary": "Amcor (AMCR) reported adjusted EPS of 95 cents, missing consensus estimates by 1.04% and declining 2.1% year-over-year due to higher energy, distribution, and interest costs. While revenues rose 6.7% to $6.13B driven by raw-material cost pass-through and volume growth, gross margins contracted to 18.9% from 19.6%. The company lowered transition-period EPS guidance to $1.70-$1.80 but reaffirmed double-digit EPS growth for 2027.",
